cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite both the software and the paper it accompanies."
title: "rfpipe: reproducible pipeline for explainable neural forecasting of rainfall-distribution shifts"
abstract: >-
  End-to-end pipeline reproducing every experiment, statistical test, table and
  result figure in "Explainable Neural Forecasting of Rainfall-Distribution
  Shifts under Hydrological Data Scarcity": divergence-target construction from
  daily reanalysis, a fourteen-model comparison under chronological splits,
  Friedman / Iman-Davenport / Nemenyi / Wilcoxon analysis with effect sizes,
  attribution diagnostics, flood-proxy validation, and an ablation of daily
  post-processing components.
type: software
license: MIT
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-10-14"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Pauli2104/Explainable-Neural-Forecasting-of-Rainfall-Distribution-Shifts-under-Hydrological-Data-Scarcity"
keywords:
  - hydrology
  - rainfall
  - distribution shift
  - explainable machine learning
  - reproducibility
  - small-sample inference
